#23750
"Gully"
"A well-worn animal track begins to wind up a narrow gully westwards here.
Tall banks of eroded earth reveal only a thin band of sky.  Straggled black
gorse tangles around pitted grey boulders, knotting them tightly to the earth.
The gully butts straight onto a wider canyon that twists southwest and
northeast below.  It would be an easy scramble down to it.
"
"climbing Watcher peak
canyon path
"
