#23802
"Collapsed Cavern"
"Dark and dry, this cavity in the smooth white stone of the mountain has a
sharp, animal reek to the air.  The back of the cavern is a pile of crushed
and broken stone, sloping sharply to the roof.  Among the fragments tattered
remnants of long-dead prey form a nest or bed.  A vee-shaped crevice angles up
to the southwest, and the air is fresher that way.
"
""
33030144 0
11 7 0
D2
""
""
0 -1 23800 0 6
A
"dig clear move"
"rock stone landslide collapss"
"act_tochar( #no, ch );
act_notchar( #ono, ch );
modify_move( ch, -100 );
"
E
"no"
"@rYou move aside some of the smaller fragments, but the large slabs are beyond
you. You give up, exhausted.@n
"
E
"ono"
"@r$n makes an attempt at moving some of the stones, but to no avail.@n
"
